{"kind":"stack","id":"shadows-stack","title":"Shadows: finding patterns in shadow size","theme":{"background":"#fdf6e3","foreground":"#1d3557","font":"Georgia, serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Shadow"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"A dark shape made when an object blocks light from reaching a surface."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-q","content":"What must be present for a shadow to form?"},{"type":"button","id":"c2-a","label":"A light source","why":"A shadow forms when an object blocks light from a light source.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"A mirror","why":"Pupils may think mirrors make shadows, but mirrors reflect light rather than block it.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-c","label":"A window","why":"Pupils may think windows let light through so the shadow is made by the glass.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"When an object moves closer to the light, what happens to its shadow?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"The shadow gets bigger","why":"Closer to the light, the object blocks more spread-out light, so the shadow grows.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"The shadow gets smaller","why":"Pupils may reverse the rule, thinking closer means less blocked light.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"The shadow disappears","why":"Pupils may think the shadow vanishes near the light, forgetting it still forms.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"When an object moves further from the light, what happens to its shadow?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"The shadow gets smaller","why":"Further from the light, the object blocks less spread-out light, so the shadow shrinks.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"The shadow gets bigger","why":"Pupils may reverse the rule and think distance makes shadows grow.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"The shadow stays the same","why":"Pupils may think distance from the light has no effect on shadow size.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"Pattern"},{"type":"text","id":"c5-e","content":"A rule that repeats: closer to the light makes a bigger shadow, further away makes a smaller one."},{"type":"button","id":"c5-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-q","content":"A torch is held near a ball, then moved further away. What happens to the shadow?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"It gets smaller","why":"Moving the torch further away means less light is blocked, so the shadow shrinks.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"It gets bigger","why":"Pupils may think moving the light away makes the shadow grow.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-c","label":"It moves to the torch","why":"Pupils may think the shadow follows the light rather than staying behind the object.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-q","content":"Ava is making shadow puppets. Should she move her hand closer to the lamp or further away to make a bigger shadow?"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-a","label":"Closer to the lamp","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Further from the lamp","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"Ava moves her hand closer. The shadow grows big on the wall. Well done, the pattern holds!"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-t","content":"Ava moves her hand further away. The shadow shrinks small. That makes it smaller, not bigger, so try again next time."},{"type":"button","id":"c9-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which change makes a shadow larger?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Moving the object closer to the light","why":"Closer to the light, the object blocks more spread-out light, so the shadow grows.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Moving the object further from the light","why":"Further from the light, the shadow shrinks, so pupils reversing the rule would pick this.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Turning the lamp off","why":"Pupils may think no light means a bigger shadow, but without light no shadow forms at all.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"You finished the shadow patterns lesson!"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Well done. Now you know that shadows get bigger when objects are closer to the light and smaller when they are further away."}],"actions":[]}}
